Z||000000||FieroGT||02-11-2000||08:57 AM||||Thanks to the wonderful (Sarcasm added) winter, my bike will be parked for another 2 months. Anyone else here live in the NE area of the country? I am so sick of snow. Thank God the SE loves this weather. <P>Anyone have any problems with their Fiero in adverse weather? I never had a problem with mine; except when the tires resembled slicks. New all season tires make my Fiero the only thing I want to drive in the winter. Imagine that, making turns without turning the steering wheel......||||reg||13
Z||000001||ChadMan||02-11-2000||09:32 AM||||Winter bites, all right.  Seems like this winter has been nothing but colds and flu, and snow and salt all over my Fiero's paint and ground into the floor mats.  The poor little car.  I can't wait to give it a good hand-washing and coat of wax.  <P>My Fiero did great in the snow until I replaced my 195/70R14 Dunlops with 215/60R14 Yokohamas.  They're great in the dry, but in more than 2" of snow, I'm the a$$hole that can't seem to get rolling when the light turns green.  Next winter I'll buy a set of beat-up 14" alloys and mount some Bridgestone Blizzaks or something similar.||||reg||8
Z||000003||Spyder||02-11-2000||06:52 PM||||Guess I shouldn’t talk about having to run the air conditioner the past few days.||||reg||1
Z||000004||superXmotorsports||02-11-2000||09:22 PM||||That's why I posted about wanting to move to Cali - I can't take this crap!  I spent a couple winters in Georgia and 1 in CA and it makes it tough to come back to the Northeast.  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||02-11-2000||10:30 PM||||I had the sunroof out yesterday.  As an Iowa refugee, I don't miss the winters up there.  I love the winters here in coastal Georgia, but hurricane season really blows!||||reg||6
Z||000007||Phaeton||02-12-2000||10:51 PM||||Its definitely springtime, pavement is showing on the larger roads, acceleration can be felt again, soon, soon the summer tires.  Yes!  Almost up to eight hours of daylight too.  Slide grab slide grab slide, positive feedback on Exactly where the tires meet the road.  Spring has got to be my fourth favorite season.<p>[This message has been edited by Phaeton (edited 02-13-2000).]||||reg||1
